Garden sheds under 2.5 metres high often don't need a planning application, based on the council's outbuilding guidance. Specifically, the shed should:

- be no more than 2.5 metres high,
- sit behind the front wall of the house, and
- cover less than half of the garden.

If your property is in a conservation area or is a listed building, different rules apply, so you should check first. If you tell me your address, I can check whether it has any planning constraints.

This is general guidance rather than a formal planning opinion. If your shed doesn't meet these conditions, or you're unsure, you should apply to the council for a decision.
